<speak>Duplicates can make a folder feel more complicated than it really is. You could use a consistent naming habit for new files without trying to reorganise every old one in a single afternoon. That keeps the project manageable. For your bank documents, preserve the original file as received and keep any personal commentary in your own separate notes. That way you can distinguish the document itself from something you've written while reading it. It also avoids confusion when you return to the folder after a while.</speak>